From 4fe014a8a7c68f02a81c465ae67c453b29f933d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Klemm <github@tklemm.eu>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 10:39:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Note in the upgrade guide that default_url_options is frozen
 unless configured

#58483 froze the default_url_options Hash that every class including the
URL helpers starts with, so changing it in place raises FrozenError
unless the application configured the options. Show the replacements.
---
 guides/source/upgrading_ruby_on_rails.md | 33 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 33 insertions(+)

diff --git a/guides/source/upgrading_ruby_on_rails.md b/guides/source/upgrading_ruby_on_rails.md
index 697bd23e7d..f9772ce683 100644
--- a/guides/source/upgrading_ruby_on_rails.md
+++ b/guides/source/upgrading_ruby_on_rails.md
@@ -147,6 +147,39 @@ warning naming each route whose controller does not exist. Such routes used to
 go unnoticed until a request matched them. Check the boot log for
 `references a missing controller` and fix or remove the routes it lists.
 
+### `default_url_options` is frozen unless configured
+
+Unless the application configures them, `default_url_options` is now a frozen
+empty Hash in controllers, mailers, integration tests, and any class that
+includes `Rails.application.routes.url_helpers`. Code that changes it in place
+raises:
+
+```ruby
+ActionMailer::Base.default_url_options[:host] = "example.com"
+# => FrozenError: can't modify frozen Hash: {}
+```
+
+Configure the options, assign a new Hash, or override the
+`default_url_options` method instead:
+
+```ruby
+# config/environments/production.rb
+config.action_mailer.default_url_options = { host: "example.com" }
+config.action_controller.default_url_options = { host: "example.com" }
+
+# or at runtime
+ActionMailer::Base.default_url_options = { host: "example.com" }
+
+# app/mailers/application_mailer.rb
+class ApplicationMailer < ActionMailer::Base
+  def default_url_options
+    { host: "example.com" }
+  end
+end
+```
+
+`Rails.application.routes.default_url_options` is not affected.
+
